---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import Newsletter from '../components/Newsletter.astro';import {site,authors,books} from '../data/catalog';
---
<Layout title="About Public Domain Pulp" description="Respect the source. Respect the genre. Make something new. Meet Public Domain Pulp, an independent publisher of original genre fiction."><header class="page-intro wrap"><p class="eyebrow">About the publisher</p><h1>The public domain<br/><em>is not a museum.</em></h1><p>Respect the source. Respect the genre. Make something new.</p></header><article class="editorial wrap"><p>Public Domain Pulp creates new fiction from public-domain characters and source material. We go back to the original stories, then ask what else these people might do, want, risk, or become.</p><p>The characters should still feel recognizably like themselves. The story should be one you have never read before.</p><h2>Familiar characters. New lives.</h2><p>A showgirl finds her voice. A sailor learns what it means to come home. Jane Porter builds a life centuries beyond the world she knows. In Calder City, familiar detectives and masked men discover how little finding the truth can settle.</p><p>Romance, screwball comedy, crime, mystery, and speculative adventure make different promises to their readers. We take those promises seriously. A familiar name may open the door; the novel has to earn the next page.</p><h2>The people on the page</h2><div class="author-list">{authors.map(a=><section class="author-card"><h3><a href={`/authors/${a.slug}/`}>{a.displayName}</a></h3><p>{[...new Set(books.filter(b=>b.contributors.some((c:any)=>c.authorId===a.id)).map(b=>b.seriesId))].length} series in the catalog</p></section>)}</div><h2 id="process">How the books are made</h2><p><strong>Human-directed. AI-assisted. Source material respected.</strong></p><p>We use AI tools in the development of these books. Direction, selection, revision, and editorial judgment determine what belongs in the finished work. Our manifesto explains the source research, continuity work, and standards behind that process.</p><p>The book still has to work on its own. The scene has to move, the joke has to land, and the reader has to care what happens next.</p><p><a class="text-link" href={site.manifesto}>Read the full manifesto on Substack ↗</a></p><h2>Independent fiction</h2><p>Public Domain Pulp is an independent publisher. References to familiar characters identify the stories and their literary ancestry; they do not indicate sponsorship or endorsement by owners of character trademarks or later adaptations.</p><p><a class="button" href="/books/">Browse the books →</a></p></article><Newsletter embedded/></Layout>
